WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
291 votes to 241.

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.460
In July 2026, the French
Parliament adopts a law

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.470
creating a new right: «l'aide à mourir».

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.150
That followed more than a year of debate.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.200
Medicine can make it possible.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.950
Parliament decides whether it is allowed.

7
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:23.370
In February 2025, Paris hosts a
summit on artificial intelligence.

8
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.610
New science, same problem.

9
00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:29.020
From Marie Curie to
«l'intelligence artificielle»:

10
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.010
who gets to set the limits on science?

11
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.720
In this mission, you'll travel
along a timeline of French science,

12
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.520
from one «découverte» to the next.

13
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.860
Then you'll argue both sides.

14
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.390
Do limits protect «la dignité humaine»?

15
00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.870
Or, as others say, «trop de
règles freinent l'innovation»?

16
00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.480
Your mission: work out who
draws the line for science,

17
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.800
and on what grounds.
